    {
        "id": "c-3",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sbg-tab",
        "g": "g-11",
        "name": "id is \"<class>:<message>\" — the name is in metadata.name",
        "info": "Identity in sbgECom is a PAIR: the manual (§2.1.1) gives MSG and CLASS as two independent\nheader bytes, and there is no revision concept. MSG 6 is EKF_EULER in class 0x00 and\nsomething else entirely in class 0x02, so the class is part of the identity.\n\nThat is why the id reads \"0:6\" and not \"6\". The log name — SBG_ECOM_LOG_EKF_EULER — is at\nmetadata.name.\n\nThese injects carry base64 because an inject node cannot hold a Buffer. A real serial, TCP\nor file node hands the parser a Buffer and needs no conversion at all.",
        "x": 300,
        "y": 180,
        "wires": []
    },
