    {
        "id": "c-12",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sbg-tab",
        "g": "g-18",
        "name": "⭐ ONE node reads BOTH protocols — nothing to configure",
        "info": "An SBG device does not wrap its NMEA output in an eCom frame. The manual is explicit\n(§2.1.4): the NMEA classes are \"only used for identification purpose and does not contain\nany sbgECom message\" — the sentences go out as raw ASCII ALONGSIDE the binary frames, on\nthe same wire. §2.1.1 Note 4 warns the integrator directly.\n\nSo this node has NO protocol setting. Fire the three injects in any order, or all of them:\nthe binary frames come out with protocol.name \"SBG ECOM\" and ids like \"0:6\", the sentence\ncomes out as \"GGA\" with protocol.name \"NMEA\", and both are CMA.\n\nThe payload rule: a string starting with $ IS the sentence. Anything else must be base64.\nA Buffer works for both, which is what a serial node gives you.",
        "x": 1080,
        "y": 180,
        "wires": []
    },
