    {
        "id": "c-19",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sbg-tab",
        "g": "g-24",
        "name": "Uptime is NOT a timestamp — fire 1/2, then 2/2",
        "info": "Almost every log starts with TIME_STAMP, and the manual calls it \"time since sensor is\npowered up\". You cannot say WHEN a sample was taken from an uptime counter, so this parser\nnever presents one as a clock.\n\nFire 1/2 first: the EKF_EULER comes out with NO metadata.timestamp.sentence, and\ncma.timestamp is just the parse time.\n\nThen fire 2/2 — a real UTC_TIME log, which publishes the counter AND the matching UTC\n(§2.3.3.2: \"you thus have to use this frame if you would like to time stamp all data to an\nabsolute UTC or GPS time reference\"). Now fire 1/2 again: the SAME frame comes out with an\nabsolute metadata.timestamp.sentence, promoted over cma.timestamp.\n\nAnything short of SBG_ECOM_UTC_VALID is refused: a guessed clock is worse than none.",
        "x": 260,
        "y": 480,
        "wires": []
    },
