    {
        "id": "c-25",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sbg-tab",
        "g": "g-30",
        "name": "Nothing vanishes — the signal is `errors`",
        "info": "A bad CRC, a wrong end flag, or bytes that are not sbgECom at all: each comes back as a\nsentence saying so, never as an empty array.\n\n\"corrupted CRC\" is the EKF_EULER frame with one CRC byte flipped — note it still decodes\nevery field, because the payload is usually fine and a silent drop is what this parser\nexists to remove.\n\n\"junk\" cannot start a frame at all: id \"unknown\", the bytes kept in raw, and one coalesced\nreport rather than a flood.\n\nAn UNMODELLED log is deliberately NOT an error — it arrives with its real id and its bytes\nat metadata.body. §2.4 lets SBG add fields to a log, so a newer device is normal.",
        "x": 1020,
        "y": 480,
        "wires": []
    },
