    {
        "id": "c-31",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sbg-tab",
        "g": "g-37",
        "name": "Memory — fire 1/2, then 2/2",
        "info": "A frame split across two serial reads only decodes if the buffer is kept. Fire 1/2: the\nfirst 20 bytes of an EKF_EULER frame produce an EMPTY array — nothing is wrong, the frame\nis simply incomplete. Then fire 2/2 with the rest and it decodes.\n\nThe memory channel reports { memory, bytes } — BYTES, because this is a binary protocol\nand a whole frame has to fit or it is flushed before its last byte arrives. The default\n4095 is exactly the largest frame the protocol allows (6 + 4086 + 3).",
        "x": 200,
        "y": 660,
        "wires": []
    },
