    {
        "id": "c-38",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sbg-tab",
        "g": "g-45",
        "name": "Ask the running node what it expects",
        "info": "These libraries run on remote installations with restricted internet access for years, so\nthe deployed binary can describe itself.\n\nids      — every sentence this build knows: the 34 eCom logs as \"<class>:<message>\" PLUS\n           every NMEA sentence id, from the one node.\ndefinition — the field table for one id, with types, units and descriptions. An eCom id\n           gets the richer answer including the log name.\nfirmware — which knowledge base is decoding, which ones exist, and `clock` once the device\n           has published a valid time. That last one answers \"why has my data no\n           timestamp?\" without guesswork.\nfake     — a real wire frame with a real CRC, as a Buffer. Deterministic, so it can live in\n           a committed flow. Wire it into another node's payload and it round-trips.",
        "x": 1000,
        "y": 660,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "i-41",
        "type": "inject",
        "z": "sbg-tab",
        "g": "g-45",
