    {
        "id": "c-46",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sbg-tab",
        "g": "g-52",
        "name": "A fake frame, fed straight back in",
        "info": "The \"fake\" channel returns a real wire frame as a Buffer: real CRC, real length. The\nfunction node moves it onto payload, and the second parser decodes it — proving the frame\nis indistinguishable from wire input.\n\nUseful for building a flow before the hardware arrives, and for a bug report: a fake is\nDETERMINISTIC, so the same request yields the same bytes forever.\n\nA fake round trip proves the FRAMING, not the field table — it is built from the same table\nit is decoded with. What catches a wrong table is the datasheet and a real capture.",
        "x": 210,
        "y": 920,
        "wires": []
    },
